Built from [stackr](https://lattice.alexnodeland.com/stackr/)'s application template (`gh:alexnodeland/lattice`) on {% if libraries == 'both' %}[artifactr](https://lattice.alexnodeland.com/artifactr/) and [reflexr](https://lattice.alexnodeland.com/reflexr/){% elif use_artifactr %}[artifactr](https://lattice.alexnodeland.com/artifactr/){% else %}[reflexr](https://lattice.alexnodeland.com/reflexr/){% endif %}{% if evals %}, with [evalr](https://lattice.alexnodeland.com/evalr/) for evaluation{% endif %}, and wired to stackr's stack: Supabase for the database and sign-in, the LiteLLM gateway for models, and OpenTelemetry, Grafana and Langfuse for telemetry and feedback.

## Quick start

You need [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/), `make`, and Docker with Compose v2. Start stackr's stack first (`make env && make up` in `packages/stackr` of a clone of [lattice](https://github.com/alexnodeland/lattice)).

```bash
git init            # the git hooks, and `copier update` later, need a repository
make install        # the dependencies (this writes uv.lock: commit it) and the git hooks
make env            # .env from .env.example; fill in the keys it asks for
make check          # lint, types and tests, as CI runs them
make up             # build the image and run it beside the stack, at http://localhost:{{ app_port }}
```

`make serve` runs it on this machine instead, with the settings in `.env`. Run `make` to list every command.

## What it serves

{% if access == 'grantr' -%}
Every surface needs a Supabase access token, or a service principal's key in its place: in the `Authorization: Bearer` header, or, for a WebSocket, a token in the `access_token` query parameter (a key goes in the header only). The token's `sub` is the user. The request names its tenant, in the `X-Tenant` header or a WebSocket's `tenant` query parameter, and may leave it out when its user is a member of one tenant only; a key names its own. Without a valid token or key it is 401. A tenant its caller isn't in, or a user in no tenant, is 403; a user in several tenants who names none is 400. Then grantr decides each command and read ([Access](#access)).
{%- else -%}
Every surface needs a Supabase access token: in the `Authorization: Bearer` header, or, for a WebSocket, in the `access_token` query parameter. The token's `sub` is the user, and its `app_metadata.tenant_id` is the tenant, whose workspaces the user can use. Anything else is 401.
{%- endif %}

| Path | What |
|---|---|
{%- if use_artifactr %}
| `/artifactr/v1` | artifactr's REST commands and reads, and its WebSocket stream (`/workspaces/{id}/stream`) |
| `/artifactr/mcp/` | artifactr's MCP server: external agents edit artifacts and talk to the agent |
{%- endif %}
{%- if use_reflexr %}
| `/reflexr/v1` | reflexr's REST publishing, reads and administration, and its WebSocket stream |
| `/reflexr/mcp/` | reflexr's MCP server: external agents publish events and operate runs |
{%- endif %}
{%- if access == 'grantr' %}
| `/grantr/v1` | grantr's admin API: tenants, members, groups, roles, grants, keys and the audit log; `/me` and `/checks` for UIs |
{%- endif %}
{%- if use_portal %}
| `/portalr/app/`, `/portalr/admin/` | [portalr](https://lattice.alexnodeland.com/portalr/)'s UIs: the app, to chat with the agents and see their work, and the admin, for access, feedback, traces, logs and spend; on when `PORTAL_SUPABASE_URL` and `PORTAL_SUPABASE_KEY` name the Supabase project they sign in to |
| `/portalr/v1` | The reads behind them, each asked of grantr first and made for the caller's tenant |
{%- endif %}
{%- if use_tracker %}
| `/relayr/v1/trackers/{tenant}/{{ tracker }}` | Where {% if tracker == 'plane' %}Plane{% else %}Vikunja{% endif %}'s webhooks reach relayr, which then reads the project at once; it needs no token, and refuses a webhook not signed with the tenant's secret |
{%- endif %}
| `/healthz` | Whether it is up, without a token |

